side_effects: "The guardian form, the energy sphere, the pooled 40 P.P.E. and 120 I.S.P., and the eight attacks of four awake minds are not on the sheet; the sheet carries one mind in its natural body."
extraction_notes: |
  Rifts World Book 3: England printed 142-144 (cache p143-p145, a text layer, page_offset 1). The natural form is printed 142-143, the Guardian 143-144; the Golden Table (144-145) is not part of the class. Read off renders of printed 143 (pools, abilities, psionics, bonuses, skills) and 152 (the ladder); every figure the cache gives agreed with the render. The Quick Find Table marks it "Ogeeyin R.C.C. (optional)" on printed 6 (cache p007), read off the text layer.
  || ID: ogeeyin. Stored as a playable R.C.C. beside the ogeeyin creature row (row 9), as an optional player race gets both.
  || FOUR MINDS: the class is ONE mind of the four. The book rolls the mental attributes, the P.P.E. and I.S.P., the two areas of knowledge and the bonuses per lobe, and gives each active lobe two attacks, so one sheet carries one lobe: attribute_dice for I.Q., M.E., M.A., P.B. and Spd, attacks_base 2, the per-lobe bonuses, 4D6x10 P.P.E. and I.S.P., two areas. The pooled +40 P.P.E. and +120 I.S.P. with all four present, the eight attacks of four awake lobes and the dormant-lobe rules are prose (Four Minds in One Body). P.S., P.P. and P.E. are not applicable to the natural body and are not stated; the sheet''s default rolls stand for them.
  || THREE FORMS: natural (the class''s own block), energy sphere and Guardian. Neither of the other two is a second_form, which carries S.D.C. and hit points only, and the Guardian''s bonuses replace rather than add to the natural form''s; both are special abilities, prose.
  || CREATURE: matches the ogeeyin creature row (row 9) on attributes, M.D.C. 1D4x100, P.P.E. and I.S.P. 4D6x10, Horror Factor 10, strike, parry, dodge and initiative. The book prints +8 to roll/pull punch; the creature row says roll with punch, and the class stores both roll and pull_punch at 8 (render read). +4 vs all magic is spell_magic and ritual_magic, as for the Chiang-Ku; +4 vs poison is toxins_poisons. The creature row''s attacks 8 is the whole body; the class''s 2 is one lobe.
  || PSIONICS: master, I.S.P. 4D6x10, no per-level gain printed. All sensitive powers: every Sensitive row the catalog holds (34), a judgement call, since later books added Sensitive powers the 1992 page could not name. Bio-regeneration (4D6 M.D.C.) is Bio-Regeneration (Super), whose 4D6 matches; Detect Psionics, Alter Aura, Death Trance, Ectoplasm and Mind Block as named. Seven super psionic powers of choice: powers_starting 7 gated to Super. No named power lacks a row.
  || SKILLS: Basic and Advanced Math and Land Navigation +20%, added to the catalog bases. The ten areas of comprehensive knowledge are skills.mos, choose 2, each option granting every skill under it at catalog base (Woodland +5%). All domestic skills are the Rifts core six (Cook, Dance, Fishing, Play Musical Instrument, Sewing, Sing), as for the Chiang-Ku. Every "all" area (Piloting, Sciences, Technical, Wilderness) is every catalog row of that category tagged rifts or untagged, a judgement call; Piloting leaves out the Robot Combat Elite rows, as printed. Pilot motor boats is Boat: Motor, Race & Hydrofoil, read sensor equipment is Sensory Equipment, basic strategies and tactics is Strategy/Tactics (a row tagged nightbane, the only one), two energy weapons or demolitions is a pick of two from W.P. Energy Pistol, W.P. Energy Rifle and Demolitions. All ancient W.P. and the modern and basic piloting lists are the ones the Chiang-Ku uses. "Recognizes the use and purpose of most devices" is a note. No secondary or related skills: an R.C.C. granting none is correct.
  || MAGIC: the Spell Magic area''s four spells from each of levels 1-6 is a Spell Magic Knowledge ability carrying a magic block of six starting groups of four; it is a pick of one against No Spell Magic, because an MOS option grants skills and nothing else, so the player takes it with the area. An MOS option must grant a skill: Spell Magic grants Lore: Magic (the principles of magic, a judgement call), and Stone Magic grants the stone-master class''s named O.C.C. skills the Ogeeyin lacks (Astronomy, Lore: Demons & Monsters, Swimming), at catalog base, a judgement call. The Stone Masters'' stone magic itself (Rifts Atlantis) is prose (Stone Magic Knowledge). Skill level seldom passing seventh is a restriction, prose.
  || XP: printed 152, the Temporal Wizard, Cernun Serpent & Ogeeyin column, read off a render; level 15 ends at 520,000.
  || MONEY AND GEAR: none, needs no material things; no starting_money, equipment_starting empty. men_of_arms false, as for every race.
  || NPC: average level 1D4+3 as a spell caster, psionic and scholar; GM Notes.
---

## Lore

The Ogeeyin look like a giant ball of flesh ten feet (3 m) across, smooth and pale pink or tan, quartered by sectioning lines. Each quarter carries two antennae and four hemispherical life nodes four inches across, and the bottom fifth is covered in foot-long black filaments. Each quarter is an individual being, and like the members of a family each shows an aptitude for something different.

One of them detected the cataclysm that created Rifts Earth. Its four minds each chose a part of the planet to study by astral projection, observed for nearly fifty years, and, sympathetic to humankind, chose to intervene. By consensus they sent one life node to England, to a geo-magnetic anomaly where it found a mysterious golden table. With the minds in the table it raised the mound, dug the tunnel and fashioned the door of the Well of Wisdom, and its essence lives in the stone Guardian that defends the Well.

**Alignment:** any, but typically Principled or Scrupulous.

**Size:** a ball 10 feet (3 m) across; the Guardian is 7 to 10 feet (2.1 to 3 m) tall.

**Weight:** 700 lbs (315 kg); the Guardian three to six tons.

**Average Life Span:** 20,000+ years.

## GM Notes

An Ogeeyin NPC is typically 1D4+3 levels as a spell caster, psionic and scholar. Each mind of a player''s Ogeeyin is a character of its own; the other three may be other players or the GM''s. It needs no equipment and has no need for material things.
